When Cursor auto-generates a Git commit message for this repository, follow Conventional Commits (https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/#specification).

## Format

<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]

## Allowed types

feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore

## Writing rules

- Write the subject in English, imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period
- Scope is optional but recommended for project areas (auth, ui, api, etc.)
- Body is optional: explain why and add context; do not repeat the diff line by line
- Breaking changes: append `!` after type/scope or add a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer
- Language: English

## Examples

fix: prevent racing of requests

Introduce a request id and a reference to latest request. Dismiss
incoming responses other than from latest request.

feat(auth): add sign-in card

fix(ui)!: remove deprecated button variants

BREAKING CHANGE: Button variant="ghost" no longer supported
